        "original_id": "253c4f91-5a54-5168-96b1-6734613ecf7d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lower Lake Stone Jail, Sulphur Bank Mine\n- Topics: quicksilver operations, mercury production, town growth, civil order, jail construction\n\nFacts:\n- From 1873 to 1883, the Sulphur Bank Mine conducted its first quicksilver operations.\n- During 1873 to 1883, rapid town growth and an urgent need for civil order led to the building of the Lower Lake Stone Jail.\n- The Sulphur Bank Mine covered 150 acres.\n- The Sulphur Bank Mine became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world.",
